# public/assets/ is NOT ignored.
#
# It was, back when the directory held build output. The art moved there in
# P3c.1 so that Vite would serve and copy it, and this line stayed — which
# meant every deployment through git silently shipped without it. Rooms
# survived only because they happened to be committed before the rule mattered.
#
# Everything under public/ is source now. It is generated by tools/art, but it
# is committed, because the generators need Python and a deployment host runs
# npm.
